    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_4c9ab67c3d73c22cc6e4e1978f29084da9788d498b5fb6c212cc4cbdb83b650d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The resonator is designed by balancing three separate resources. Square-free weights on logarithmic prime bands create a large multiplicative divisor statistic. Occupancy caps remove over- and under-populated band configurations so that the retained divisor-closed set has cardinality at most N, while exponential tilting shows that the exceptional weighted mass is negligible. Finally, geometric cells of relative width about 1/T replace each occupied cell by one representative and aggregate nearby squared weights; in the Gaussian Fourier expansion, rapid decay suppresses separated cells, while a Cauchy-Schwarz comparison transfers exact relations in the original support to approximate relations among the representatives.",
